          "text": "A big drop is formed by coalescing $1000$ small droplets of water. The ratio of surface energy of $1000$ droplets to that of energy of big drop is $\\frac{10}x$. The value of $x$ is ____",
          "solution": "Volume conservation: $1000\\cdot\\frac43\\pi r^3=\\frac43\\pi R^3\\Rightarrow R=10r$.<br>Surface energy of the small droplets $=1000\\times4\\pi r^2T$; of the big drop $=4\\pi(10r)^2T=100\\times4\\pi r^2T$.<br>Ratio $=\\frac{1000}{100}=10=\\frac{10}x\\Rightarrow x=1$."
