          "solution": "The point $P$ lies between the sheets at $x=a$ ($-2\\sigma$) and $x=3a$ ($+\\sigma$). Each sheet gives a field $\\frac{|\\text{charge density}|}{2\\epsilon_0}$, directed towards a negative sheet and away from a positive one.<br>$-\\sigma$ at $x=-a$ (to the left of $P$): towards it, i.e. $-x$ direction, $\\frac{\\sigma}{2\\epsilon_0}$.<br>$-2\\sigma$ at $x=a$ (to the left of $P$): towards it, $-x$ direction, $\\frac{2\\sigma}{2\\epsilon_0}$.<br>$+\\sigma$ at $x=3a$ (to the right of $P$): away from it, $-x$ direction, $\\frac{\\sigma}{2\\epsilon_0}$.<br>Total $=\\frac{(1+2+1)\\sigma}{2\\epsilon_0}=\\frac{2\\sigma}{\\epsilon_0}\\Rightarrow x=2$."
